        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "Buying a Treadmill on Amazon", item: "https://www.treadmillreviewsusa.com/buying-a-treadmill-on-amazon/" },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      mainEntity: [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Is it safe to buy a treadmill on Amazon?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Generally yes, provided you check who the seller is, confirm the specification against the manufacturer's own figures, and read the delivery and return terms on the specific listing. The risks are inaccurate listings, pooled reviews and the practical difficulty of returning a heavy item, not the marketplace itself.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Are Amazon treadmills good?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Amazon sells treadmills from established manufacturers alongside many lesser-known brands, so quality ranges from very good to very basic. Judge each machine on continuous horsepower, running surface, maximum user weight, warranty and parts availability rather than on the star rating or the listing title.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Can you return a treadmill to Amazon?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually, but the terms depend on the listing and the seller, and large items can carry their own conditions. Returns of heavy machines commonly involve scheduling a pickup and may require repacking. Check the return terms on the product page before ordering, and keep the box until you are sure.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Does Amazon deliver treadmills to your room?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "It depends on the listing. Smaller machines may arrive as ordinary parcels left at the door. Larger treadmills are often delivered by a freight or large-item carrier, and the service may stop at the kerb or door unless room-of-choice delivery is included or offered. Read the delivery details on the listing.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "Who handles the warranty on a treadmill bought on Amazon?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Usually the manufacturer. Register the machine if the manufacturer asks you to, keep your order confirmation as proof of purchase, and check before buying that the manufacturer honours its warranty for the seller you are buying from, since some limit coverage to authorised retailers.",
          },
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          name: "What should I look for in an Amazon treadmill machine listing?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Look for the continuous motor rating rather than peak horsepower, the belt width and length of the running surface, the maximum user weight, whether incline is powered, the model number and the seller. Confirm those figures on the manufacturer's website, since listing details are sometimes out of date.",
          },
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      description: description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Morgan Reyes" },
      datePublished: "2026-10-06",
      dateModified: "2026-10-06",
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Treadmill Reviews USA" },
    },
  ],
